{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"18. Stains","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp235-255'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 235–255 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Malavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>18. Stains </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>The Contaminant Chapter </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp235'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Goghātakaputtavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paṇḍupalāsova dānisi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Today you’re like a withered leaf, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Now you are like a fallen leaf, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yamapurisāpi ca te upaṭṭhitā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Yama’s men await you. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and Death's minions are near. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uyyogamukhe ca tiṭṭhasi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You stand at the departure gates, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>You stand at the starting point of a struggle, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pātheyyampi ca te na vijjati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>yet you have no supplies for the road. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and no provisions can be found for you. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp236'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>So karohi dīpamattano, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Make an island of yourself! </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Make an island for yourself, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Khippaṁ vāyama paṇḍito bhava; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Swiftly strive, learn to be wise! </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>quickly try to become wise; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Niddhantamalo anaṅgaṇo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Purged of stains, flawless, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who has no contaminants and no flaws </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dibbaṁ ariyabhūmiṁ upehisi. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ll go to the heavenly realm of the noble ones. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>will reach the divine state of the noble ones. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp237'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Upanītavayo ca dānisi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You’ve journeyed the stages of life, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Now you are close to departing; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sampayātosi yamassa santikaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and now you set out to meet Yama. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>you are in the presence of Death. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vāso te natthi antarā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Along the way there’s nowhere to stay, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>You have nowhere to dwell here, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pātheyyampi ca te na vijjati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>yet you have no supplies for the road. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and no provisions can be found for you. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp238'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>So karohi dīpamattano, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Make an island of yourself! </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Make an island for yourself, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Khippaṁ vāyama paṇḍito bhava; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Swiftly strive, learn to be wise! </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>quickly try to become wise; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Niddhantamalo anaṅgaṇo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Purged of stains, flawless, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who has no contaminants and no flaws </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na punaṁ jātijaraṁ upehisi. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ll not come again to rebirth and old age. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>does not come again to birth and decrepitude. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp239'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aññatarabrāhmaṇavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Anupubbena medhāvī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A smart person would purge </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Progressively, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>thokaṁ thokaṁ khaṇe khaṇe; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>their own stains gradually, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>bit by bit, moment after moment, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kammāro rajatasseva, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>bit by bit, moment by moment, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>like a smith purifying silver, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niddhame malamattano. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a smith smelting silver. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the wise remove their contaminants. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp240'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Tissattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ayasāva malaṁ samuṭṭhitaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It is the rust born on the iron </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When rust appears </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tatuṭṭhāya tameva khādati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that eats away the place it arose. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>it eats away the metal that produced it; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ atidhonacārinaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>And so it is their own deeds </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>in the same way, a sanctimonious person </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sāni kammāni nayanti duggatiṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that lead the overly-ascetic to a bad place. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is led to a bad destination by their own actions. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp241'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Lāḷudāyīvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Asajjhāyamalā mantā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Not rehearsing is the stain of hymns. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Non-repetition contaminates mantras, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>anuṭṭhānamalā gharā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The stain of houses is neglect. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>non-upkeep contaminates a house, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Malaṁ vaṇṇassa kosajjaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Laziness is the stain of beauty. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>laziness contaminates beauty, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pamādo rakkhato malaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A guard’s stain is negligence. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>negligence contaminates security. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp242'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Aññatarakulaputtavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Malitthiyā duccaritaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Misconduct is a woman’s stain. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Misconduct contaminates a woman, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>maccheraṁ dadato malaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>A giver’s stain is stinginess. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>stinginess contaminates a donor, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Malā ve pāpakā dhammā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Bad qualities are a stain </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>evil choices contaminate </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>asmiṁ loke paramhi ca. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in this world and the next. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>both this life and the next. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp243'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tato malā malataraṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But a worse stain than these </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>There is a contaminant that is even worse than that: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>avijjā paramaṁ malaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is ignorance, the worst stain of all. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>ignorance, the paramount contaminant. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Etaṁ malaṁ pahantvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having given up that stain, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Abandon this contaminant </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nimmalā hotha bhikkhavo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>be without stains, mendicants! </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and be free of contaminants, monks! </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp244'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Cūḷasāribhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sujīvaṁ ahirikena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Life is easy for the shameless. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is easy to lose one's conscience, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kākasūrena dhaṁsinā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>With all the rude courage of a crow, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>to act like an impudent and offensive crow, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pakkhandinā pagabbhena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they live pushy, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>obtrusive and inconsiderate, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>saṅkiliṭṭhena jīvitaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>rude, and corrupt. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>living a defiled life. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp245'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Hirīmatā ca dujjīvaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Life is hard for the conscientious, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is not easy to maintain one's conscience, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ sucigavesinā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always seeking purity, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>always seeking to be impeccable, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Alīnenāppagabbhena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>neither clinging nor rude, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one who is diligent and considerate, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>suddhājīvena passatā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>pure of livelihood and discerning. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>insightful and living a life of purity. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp246'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcaupāsakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yo pāṇamatipāteti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Take anyone in this world </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who kills, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>musāvādañca bhāsati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who kills living creatures, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>lies, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Loke adinnamādiyati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>speaks falsely, steals, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>steals, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>paradārañca gacchati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>commits adultery, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>commits adultery, </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp247'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Surāmerayapānañca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and indulges in drinking </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and drinks alcohol - </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yo naro anuyuñjati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>beer and wine. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a person who engages in such activities </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Idheva meso lokasmiṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Right here they dig up </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>right here in this world </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mūlaṁ khaṇati attano. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the root of their own self. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>destroys their own foundation. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp248'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ bho purisa jānāhi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Know this, my man: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Therefore, you should know </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pāpadhammā asaññatā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they are unrestrained and wicked. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>that lack of restraint is evil; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mā taṁ lobho adhammo ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Don’t let that greed and unrighteousness </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>do not let greed contrary to Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ciraṁ dukkhāya randhayuṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>inflict pain on you for long. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>afflict you with long-lasting suffering. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp249'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Tissadaharavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dadāti ve yathāsaddhaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The people give according to their faith, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>People give because it brings </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yathāpasādanaṁ jano; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>according to their confidence. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>faith and joy. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tattha yo ca maṅku bhavati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>If you get upset over that, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who is disturbed </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>paresaṁ pānabhojane; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>over others’ food and drink, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when food and drink are given to others </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na so divā vā rattiṁ vā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ll not, by day or by night, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>does not gain concentration </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samādhimadhigacchati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>become immersed in samādhi. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp250'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yassa cetaṁ samucchinnaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Those who have cut that out, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has shredded, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mūlaghaccaṁ samūhataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>dug it up at the root, eradicated it, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>uprooted, and destroyed that attitude </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sa ve divā vā rattiṁ vā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they will, by day or by night, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>gains concentration </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samādhimadhigacchati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>become immersed in samādhi. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>by day and by night. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp251'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcaupāsakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Natthi rāgasamo aggi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>There is no fire like greed, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>There is no fire as strong as passion, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi dosasamo gaho; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>no crime like hate, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>no grasp as strong as aversion, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Natthi mohasamaṁ jālaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>no net like delusion, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>no trap as strong as delusion, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi taṇhāsamā nadī. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>no river like craving. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>no river as strong as craving. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp252'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Meṇḍakaseṭṭhivatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sudassaṁ vajjamaññesaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>It’s easy to see the faults of others, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>It is easy to see the faults of others, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>attano pana duddasaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>hard to see one’s own. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and hard to see our own. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paresaṁ hi so vajjāni, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>For the faults of others </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When we frequently expose </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>opunāti yathā bhusaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>are tossed high like hay, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the faults of others </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Attano pana chādeti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>while one’s own are hidden, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>but conceal our own, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kaliṁva kitavā saṭho. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as a cheat hides a bad hand. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>we are like a fraud cheating at dice. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp253'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Ujjhānasaññittheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Paravajjānupassissa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When you look for the flaws of others, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When one looks at the faults of others </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ ujjhānasaññino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always finding fault, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and is always looking to criticize, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Āsavā tassa vaḍḍhanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>your defilements only grow, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one's defilements grow </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ārā so āsavakkhayā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’re far from ending defilements. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and one is far the elimination of defilements. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp254'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Subhaddaparibbājakavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ākāseva padaṁ natthi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>In the atmosphere there is no track, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>There is no path in the sky, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samaṇo natthi bāhire; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>there’s no true ascetic outside here. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>there is no contemplative elsewhere. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Papañcābhiratā pajā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>People enjoy proliferation, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>People delight in complication, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nippapañcā tathāgatā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the Realized Ones are free of proliferation. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>whereas a Truth-Finder is free of complication. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp255'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ākāseva padaṁ natthi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>In the atmosphere there is no track, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>There is no path in the sky, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>samaṇo natthi bāhire; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>there’s no true ascetic outside here. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>there is no contemplative elsewhere. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅkhārā sassatā natthi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>No conditions last forever, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>There is nothing that is eternal, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>natthi buddhānamiñjitaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the Awakened Ones are not shaken. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and no agitation in Buddhas. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Malavaggo aṭṭhārasamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
